<p>The obvious trade is harmonic/RV reducers. The less obvious derivative i=
s what constrains reducer capacity expansion: ultra-precision grinding, enc=
oder gratings, bearings, metrology and force-torque sensor manufacturing. I=
ndustry reporting shows reducer orders booked into 2027 while Chinese local=
ization is already increasing quickly, implying that simply owning reducer =
makers risks being late to the bottleneck.</p>
<p>The research direction should therefore be: reducer demand -&gt; capacit=
y additions -&gt; precision-machine-tool and inspection demand. This is exa=
ctly the bottleneck-derivative framework: find what becomes scarce when tod=
ay=E2=80=99s shortage is successfully addressed.</p>
